  "notes": "Image 1 (front): label is the Renesas port name (Pad# column, e.g. P401) treated as the GPIO name; silkscreen/gray label first in functions, then digital Dnn and peripheral names read outward. Power pins use the printed power names (VUSB, VREF, 3V3) with silkscreen/alternate spellings in functions. Skipped: Qwiic and JST battery connectors (pins not individually labeled), RGB/STAT LEDs, USR button, internal DA14531MOD-RA6M5 UART and VREF Enable/USR pad callouts that are not header pins. Image 2 (back): headers recorded from silkscreen only (VR printed for VREF). The microSD socket, QSPI flash and IC callouts (RT9080, MAX17048, LM66200, MCP73831) are not wiring points and were skipped."
